  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "Restless steppe riders who keep no city longer than the grass wishes to hold it.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Zhurani map the world by wells, star currents, and remembered horse-trails rather than by roads or borders. Every hearth is temporary, every oath tied to a person rather than a seat, and every bargain hedged with wit. They are famous for lavish guest-gifts and sudden disappearances, for a Zhurani host leaves before a ruler can imagine taxing it."
